+**6. Links.** A folder or file link (Drive, Dropbox, WeTransfer, Frame.io) is stored as given under "## Guest assets", in a line of the same shape with "link" in place of the type, bytes and sha256, keyed "<message key>#link<n>". This run has no authorised way to download from those services, so copying the link is not storing the files: the pending line stays open with reason "link only: files not stored".
+a. Owner. Production files for an episode go to Sarika, the production default. A link to something that isn't production material never reaches this page (section 2 routes it to its own Task row or Deal).
+b. One Task per open obligation. Before creating, look for an open Engagement row Kind Task (Task state not Done or On hold) with For engagement this Engagement and Next action starting "Sarika: save". None: create one, Kind Task, Show the Engagement's Show (the same Show as the Episode; if they differ, create nothing and report "show mismatch"; AD Personal only for work that belongs to no show), For engagement this Engagement, Waiting on Sarika, Task state Handed over, Next action "Sarika: save <guest>'s linked files to the <D Mon> Episode: put each file under its link line in Guest assets, or write on the link line why not". One open Task covers every open link line of that Engagement.
+c. Closing a link line needs evidence on the Episode, never the Task's state alone: file blocks directly under the link line (each then gets its own line with filename, bytes and sha256, computed by downloading the block as in 5b), or a dated disposition a person wrote on the link line ("not needed", "expired, asked again", with name and date). Then mark the pending line "filed <date>" or "closed: <disposition>".
+d. Task marked Done but no files and no disposition: keep the pending line open, set that Task back to Handed over once, with Next action "Sarika: <guest>'s linked files aren't on the Episode yet: add them under the link line, or write why not", and say so in the report. If it comes back Done again with nothing on the Episode, leave it and report it every run.
 
 **7. Retries and limits.** Every run takes open "## Assets to file" lines first, oldest first, then new mail. Open lines have no age limit, so work outside the read window is still done. At most 5 uploads a run. If a run stops after an upload but before the page write, the upload expires and the next run uploads again. If it stops after the page write but before marking the pending line, 5b finds the file and only marks the line. A failed file never marks anything filed and never closes another file's line.
 
